Let LIST be a datatype for an implementation of linked list defined as follows:
```c
typedef struct list {
    int data;
    struct list *next;
} LIST;
```

Suppose a program has created two linked lists, L1 and L2. L1 contains 9 nodes with values: 1,7,12,3,9,5,11,15,8. L2 contains 7 nodes with values: 1,11,6,9,15,12,4.

Consider the following C program segment that modifies the list L1:
```c
int find (int query, LIST *list) {
    while (list != NULL){
        if(list->data == query) return 1;
        list = list->next;
    }
    return 0;
}
int main () {
    ptr1=L1; ptr2=L2;
    while (ptr1->next != NULL){
        query = ptr1->next->data;
        if (find (query, L2))
            ptr1->next = ptr1->next->next;
        else ptr1 = ptr1->next;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

